// REJECTS: Field 'specification' should be specified only once
//
// A connection takes exactly one datasource specification. The parser rule is an unordered
// `( ... )*`, so ORDER is free but REPETITION is not -- the constraint lives in the walker,
// in validateAndExtractRequiredField, not in the grammar.
//
// The mirror of exclusive-two-auth-strategies.pure, and deliberately so: `auth` and
// `specification` are validated by two different call sites, and a rewrite that enforces
// "only once" for one field and not the other passes whichever fixture it happens to
// implement. A parser generated straight from the .g4 accepts both files.
###Connection
RelationalDatabaseConnection fixture::neg::TwoSpecs
{
   store: fixture::neg::Db;
   type: H2;
   specification: LocalH2 {  };
   specification: Static { name: 'db'; host: 'h'; port: 1234; };
   auth: DefaultH2;
}
